# selections — Ring-1 stratum: declarative selections, matcher-inert (C8/F11)
stratum selections "Selections as declarative data. No predicate language exists or will (C8, law): a selection names what was chosen and why; anything requiring evaluation routes to via."

enum reason "Why a selection exists." { threshold-crossed schedule manual delegated }

record selection "A declared choice of subjects for an intent — data the matcher carries without evaluating (the C8 vector: 'a selection manifest matched without evaluation')." {
    subject-prefix : name "The chosen subject prefix (F3: stream subjects are prefixes)."
    intent : text "The intent this selection feeds."
    why : term-of reason "The declared reason — an enum, never an expression."
}
